WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.340
Here's a newborn.

2
00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:04.080
It can cry, feed and sleep.

3
00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:06.900
It has no idea what shoplifting is.

4
00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:09.280
Fast forward to age 14.

5
00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:10.730
A shopping centre.

6
00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:14.490
An older teenager slips a
cap into a bag and walks out.

7
00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:15.940
The group laughs.

8
00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:18.010
The younger teen is watching.

9
00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:19.270
Closely.

10
00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:22.160
Nobody is born knowing how to shoplift.

11
00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:23.710
So who teaches it?

12
00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:26.740
In this mission, you'll
meet social learning theory:

13
00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:29.900
the idea that we pick up
behaviour, including crime,

14
00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:31.420
from watching others.

15
00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:33.800
You'll find out who
counts as a role model,

16
00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:36.320
and why it matters who we want to be like.

17
00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:40.640
And you'll ask whether it matters
what happens to the role model next.

18
00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:44.280
Your mission: work out who
teaches crime, and how.
